  "Question": "A high-speed train travels at 300 km/h. Which of the following correctly describes the relationship between the distance s km and the time t needed to travel that distance? (The unit of t is h.)",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(t=300s\\)",
    "B": "\\(t=300/s\\)",
    "C": "\\(t=s-300\\)",
    "D": "\\(t=s/300\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Time = distance ÷ speed. When the speed is fixed, \\(t=s/300\\), so t is directly proportional to s. Option B reverses the positions of speed and distance.",
